      "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n`FixFunctionalizationPass` defunctionalizes `rms_norm_dynamic_per_token_quant` but not `rms_norm_per_block_quant`, which the norm + quant fusion emits for block-FP8 models. Inductor then copies the residual in every layer. Both ops mutate the same arguments, so this adds the per-block op to the existing branch, which should save a little decode time on block-FP8 models. Possibly the extra kernel in #37832.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Removes one residual copy kernel per layer per decode step.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- New case `TestFusedAddRMSNormBlockQuant` in `tests/compile/passes/test_functionalization.py` fails on main and passes with this PR.\r\n- H100 NVL, `Qwen/Qwen3-8B-FP8`, batch 8: the copy (`triton_poi_fused_0`, 36 per step) took 0.054 ms of each 7.3 ms decode step on main and is gone with this PR.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nAI usage: Claude Code helped with the test runs. I traced the issue, chose the fix, and validated every change.\r\n",
