    {
      "body": "Measured the copy this removes. Setup: Qwen3-8B-FP8, H100 SXM5, vLLM main `e8e1e961`, `fuse_norm_quant` + `DeepGemmFp8BlockScaledMMKernel`.\r\n\r\nThe copy appears as `triton_poi_fused_0`:\r\n- 36 launches per decode step, 1.2–2.2 µs each\r\n- **45 / 56 / 80 µs per step at bs 1 / 32 / 256**\r\n- 43–60% of the whole norm+quant-fusion regression at bs ≥ 32\r\n\r\nTraces and scripts: https://github.com/daniildiveev/llm-inference-perf-notes/blob/845e7c62b79f1d6dcaa7433961b5931dbfca56da/2026-10-15_h100sxm_fusion-remeasure/RESULTS.md",
      "created_at": "2026-10-16T18:50:17Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60481#issuecomment-6222474337",
      "id": 6222474337,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:50:17Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "daniildiveev"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@ProExpertProg Could you review this and comment /ci run? The full CI has not run since this opened. It adds rms_norm_per_block_quant to an existing branch in fix_functionalization.py. The new test fails on main. daniildiveev measured the residual copy this removes on an H100: 45, 56 and 80 µs per decode step at batch sizes 1, 32 and 256.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-01T21:18:53Z",
